## Why this satisfies the check
The outcome step now carries one specific measurable criterion — the exact
message `Hello, Alice` — which a step definition can assert against the
command's standard output. The behaviour specified is unchanged: the greeter
still greets the person whose name it is given; the step now says so in terms
a run can settle, naming the greeting text and the name together. The verb
`prints` is the observable action the product document's vocabulary asks for,
and the wording introduces no forbidden qualifier or forbidden action.

